# Round 74 — Euler products inside the critical strip (all pass the Davenport–Heilbronn filter)

| item | relation to RH | verdict |
|------|----------------|---------|
| Conrad 2005: partial products converge at a point of Re s = 1/2 | ⇒ RH | open: convergence unproved |
| Gonek 2012: finite Euler products approximate ζ on Re s > 1/2 | ≡ RH | CIRCULAR |
| Gonek–Hughes–Keating hybrid product | proved under RH | CIRCULAR |
| Littlewood: Euler product converges on Re s > 1/2 | ≡ RH | CIRCULAR |
| Goldfeld / Kuo–Murty partial products (BSD form) | not RH-equivalent | DEAD |
| Akatsuka–Kaneko critical-line asymptotics | under RH | CIRCULAR |
| Euler product + functional equation | convergence on Re s > 1/2 ⇒ RH | CIRCULAR |
| Rubinstein–Sarnak races | under GRH + LI | DEAD |

These are the only criteria seen so far that are Euler-product-sensitive by construction, yet each needs
convergence of the product inside the strip, which is itself RH-strength.
